            <p class="last-updated">📅 <strong>Last Updated:</strong> August 05, 2026</p>

            <h2 id="privacy-policy-heading">Privacy Policy</h2>
            <p>At <strong>Periodic Instructor</strong> (a part of <strong>ASR Group</strong>), we value your privacy. This policy explains how we handle your information when you visit our website. It aligns with international standards like <strong>GDPR</strong>, <strong>CCPA</strong>, <strong>COPPA</strong>, and the <strong>ePrivacy Directive</strong>.</p>

            <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
            <h3>1.1 Personal Information</h3>
            <p>We may collect information you voluntarily provide when you contact us (e.g., via email or a form):</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Identifiers:</strong> Name, email address, or other details you share.</li>
                <li><strong>Communication Content:</strong> The messages you send us.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>1.2 Non-Personal Information</h3>
            <p>We automatically collect non-identifiable data such as:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Browser type, operating system, referring pages, date/time stamps, clickstream data.</li>
                <li>Aggregated usage statistics that do not identify you personally.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>2. How We Collect Information</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Directly from you:</strong> when you submit a form or send an email.</li>
                <li><strong>Automatically:</strong> through cookies, server logs, and similar technologies.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>3. Legal Basis for Processing (GDPR)</h2>
            <p>If you are in the European Economic Area (EEA), we process personal data based on:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Your consent,</strong> which you can withdraw anytime.</li>
                <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> to improve our services and ensure security.</li>
                <li><strong>Legal obligations</strong> if required by law.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>4. How We Use Your Information</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>To respond to your inquiries and provide support.</li>
                <li>To improve our website, content, and user experience.</li>
                <li>To analyse usage trends and maintain site security.</li>
                <li>To comply with legal obligations.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>5. Data Retention</h2>
            <p>We keep your personal information only as long as needed for the purposes described here, then securely delete or anonymise it. Retention periods vary based on data type and legal requirements.</p>

            <h2>6. Your Data Protection Rights</h2>
            <h3>6.1 GDPR Rights (EEA users)</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Access, correct, or delete your data.</li>
                <li>Restrict or object to processing.</li>
                <li>Data portability.</li>
                <li>Withdraw consent.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>6.2 CCPA Rights (California residents)</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Know what personal information we collect, use, or disclose.</li>
                <li>Request deletion of your information.</li>
                <li>Opt-out of sale (we do not sell your personal information).</li>
                <li>Not be discriminated against for exercising your rights.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>7. Do Not Sell My Personal Information</h2>
            <p>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information.</p>

            <h2>8. International Data Transfers</h2>
            <p>Your data may be processed in a country other than your own. We take appropriate steps to ensure your information remains protected according to this policy and applicable laws.</p>

            <h2>9. Data Breach Notification</h2>
            <p>If a breach occurs that risks your rights, we will notify the relevant authorities and affected individuals without undue delay, as required by law.</p>

            <h2>10. Children's Privacy</h2>
            <p>Our website is not directed to children under 13 (or 16 in the EEA). We do not knowingly collect data from children. If we learn a child has provided personal data, we will delete it promptly.</p>

            <h2>11. Third-Party Services & External Links</h2>
            <p>We may use third-party services (such as hosting or analytics tools) that collect non-personal usage data. These services have their own privacy policies. Our website may link to external sites; we are not responsible for their content or privacy practices.</p>

            <h2>12. Changes to This Policy</h2>
            <p>We may update this policy. Material changes will be posted here with a new "Last Updated" date. Please review it periodically.</p>

            <div class="contact-box">
